WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.694 --> 00:00:14.935
hundred years passed.

2
00:00:16.196 --> 00:00:18.518
Wukong stayed trapped under the mountain.

3
00:00:19.899 --> 00:00:22.341
A thick layer of moss covered the monkey.

4
00:00:25.704 --> 00:00:30.448
One day Buddha sat in the Thunderclap Monastery in the Western Paradise.

5
00:00:31.508 --> 00:00:32.929
He was talking to his students.

6
00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:39.313
"The people in the East, in the Tang Empire, need our help," said Buddha.

7
00:00:41.054 --> 00:00:43.016
lie, cheat, and steal.

8
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.638
They are greedy and constantly fighting."

9
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.821
held up a bundle of scrolls.

10
00:00:50.841 --> 00:00:53.983
"These are the True Scriptures.

11
00:00:54.964 --> 00:00:57.806
They will teach the people in the East to act better."

12
00:00:59.347 --> 00:01:01.168
"Wonderful," said one student.

13
00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:04.033
"Let's bring the scriptures to the Tang Empire."

14
00:01:05.773 --> 00:01:06.454
shook his head.

15
00:01:06.474 --> 00:01:08.614
"No," he said.

16
00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:14.136
"A true believer—a monk—needs to come here to get them.

17
00:01:15.877 --> 00:01:18.678
Will anyone go to the East to find a worthy monk?"

18
00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:22.179
stepped forward.

19
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.860
"I will go."

20
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:33.821
The Tang Emperor smiled as his head monk read to a small group of people.

21
00:01:35.002 --> 00:01:37.482
The monk was reading old religious texts.

22
00:01:38.863 --> 00:01:40.243
A woman interrupted the monk.

23
00:01:41.423 --> 00:01:43.664
"Why are you reading those old texts?"

24
00:01:44.064 --> 00:01:44.604
she asked.

25
00:01:44.624 --> 00:01:48.165
"Don't you know about the True Scriptures?"

26
00:01:50.946 --> 00:01:51.846
emperor stood up.

27
00:01:51.866 --> 00:01:57.948
"How dare you interrupt okay," said the monk.

28
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:10.347
He walked over to the "What are the True Scriptures?"

29
00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:13.189
woman looked at the monk carefully.

30
00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:16.771
"They contain many lessons.

31
00:02:17.972 --> 00:02:21.314
People who learn the lessons never have to suffer again."

32
00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:23.756
"Do you have them here?"

33
00:02:24.156 --> 00:02:24.797
asked the monk.

34
00:02:27.138 --> 00:02:27.699
said the woman.

35
00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:31.200
"They are with Buddha in the Western Paradise.

36
00:02:32.561 --> 00:02:36.062
Someone must travel to the Thunderclap Monastery to get them.

37
00:02:37.102 --> 00:02:40.243
But only a true believer may make the journey."

38
00:02:42.223 --> 00:02:44.104
took a robe out of her bag.

39
00:02:44.124 --> 00:02:46.545
"Put this on."

40
00:02:50.046 --> 00:02:51.326
The monk put on the robe.

41
00:02:53.126 --> 00:02:54.567
of light shone from it.

42
00:02:55.707 --> 00:02:59.016
The emperor gasped.

43
00:02:59.357 --> 00:03:01.118
are a true believer," said the woman.

44
00:03:02.299 --> 00:03:04.021
"Will you make the journey?"

45
00:03:04.101 --> 00:03:09.686
"Yes," said the monk, looking down at the glowing robe.

46
00:03:09.706 --> 00:03:11.627
"It will be an honor."

47
00:03:12.928 --> 00:03:15.811
"The journey will be very difficult," said the woman.

48
00:03:17.292 --> 00:03:20.915
"Wide rivers and steep mountains will block your path.

49
00:03:22.177 --> 00:03:25.720
Fierce creatures and evil demons will try to attack you.

50
00:03:29.204 --> 00:03:32.247
But don't fear—you will have help from me."

51
00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:37.412
Suddenly the room filled with blinding light.

52
00:03:38.653 --> 00:03:41.516
The woman rose into the air and changed form.

53
00:03:41.536 --> 00:03:44.719
"It's the bodhisattva Guanyin!"

54
00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:45.880
someone cried.

55
00:03:46.982 --> 00:03:49.244
The emperor and everyone else in the room bowed.

56
00:03:50.485 --> 00:03:53.308
Guanyin rose higher and then disappeared.

57
00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.581
The next morning there was a huge feast.

58
00:04:01.102 --> 00:04:03.303
The Tang Emperor sat next to the monk.

59
00:04:03.323 --> 00:04:07.826
"Your journey will help our empire greatly," said the emperor.

60
00:04:07.846 --> 00:04:13.288
"No longer will our people suffer or treat each other badly.

61
00:04:14.509 --> 00:04:17.471
From now on, I will think of you as my brother.

62
00:04:18.771 --> 00:04:20.953
You will be called the Tang Monk."

63
00:04:20.973 --> 00:04:24.234
"Thank you, Your Majesty," said the Tang Monk.

64
00:04:24.254 --> 00:04:27.176
"How long will the journey take?"

65
00:04:27.644 --> 00:04:28.404
asked the emperor.

66
00:04:28.424 --> 00:04:32.065
"I will return in a few years," said the monk.

67
00:04:37.747 --> 00:04:40.928
Later that day the Tang Monk got ready for his journey.

68
00:04:42.588 --> 00:04:44.789
put the special robe into a bag.

69
00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.231
He put dried foods into another bag.

70
00:04:53.651 --> 00:04:56.052
A big crowd gathered to say good-bye.

71
00:04:57.548 --> 00:04:59.970
"Good luck, my brother," said the Tang Emperor.

72
00:05:02.332 --> 00:05:06.095
The Tang Monk climbed onto a horse and rode toward the West.

73
00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:15.463
He had traveled for over a month when he came to a big mountain.

74
00:05:17.604 --> 00:05:20.146
Slowly his horse walked up a steep trail.

75
00:05:21.828 --> 00:05:23.869
have a bad feeling," said the Tang Monk.

76
00:05:25.411 --> 00:05:27.644
He looked around uneasily.

77
00:05:27.704 --> 00:05:29.166
"I hope there aren't any demons here."

78
00:05:30.927 --> 00:05:35.792
Suddenly a voice boomed, "Who is walking on my mountain?"
